Example using Amazon Web Services ecosystem.:

1. Real Production Architecture
External API (sales/orders API)
⬇
Python script extracts data
⬇
Store raw data in Amazon Web Services S3
⬇
Load into data warehouse (Amazon Web Services Redshift)
⬇
Dashboard tools analyze data
Used for:
      business reports
      dashboards
      analytics
      
2. Step 1 – Fetch Data from API
Example: Get sales data from API.

      import requests
      import pandas as pd
       
      url = "https://api.company.com/orders"
       
      response = requests.get(url)
      data = response.json()
       
      df = pd.DataFrame(data)
       
      print(df.head())
Now API data is stored in Pandas DataFrame.

3. Step 2 – Transform Data
Example cleaning and processing.

      df["total_amount"] = df["price"] * df["quantity"]
       
      df = df[df["status"] == "completed"]
      
4. Step 3 – Store Raw Data in Cloud Storage
Upload file to Amazon Web Services S3.

      import boto3
       
      df.to_csv("orders.csv", index=False)
       
      s3 = boto3.client("s3")
       
      s3.upload_file(
          "orders.csv",
          "analytics-data-bucket",
          "orders/orders.csv"
      )
Now data is stored in cloud data lake.

5. Step 4 – Load Data to Data Warehouse
Data from Amazon Web Services S3 is loaded into Amazon Web Services Redshift for analytics queries.
Example query in warehouse:

COPY orders
FROM 's3://analytics-data-bucket/orders/orders.csv'
IAM_ROLE 'arn:aws:iam::xxxx:role/redshift-role'
CSV;

